---
[goal]
Make sure we keep the existing cart_v2 cookie name and never store PII in the payload.

[context]
- What was diagnosed:
  - Found it. sessionStorage is cleared by the cross-origin redirect back from Stripe, so CartService.hydrate() reads null on the first paint.
  - The hydrate call currently costs 450ms and the edge returns a 503 when it misses.
- Decisions reached:
  - We're going with a signed cookie instead: move hydration into src/middleware.ts so it runs before React mounts.
  - Decision: read the cart from a signed cookie in middleware, keeping CartService.hydrate() as the public entry point so the API is unchanged.
- Files in play: src/api/stripe-webhook.ts, src/checkout/CartService.ts, src/middleware.ts, tests/checkout_refresh.spec.ts
- References:
  - https://example.com/docs/signed-cart

[constraints]
- You must not change the public CartService API, and don't touch the webhook handler in src/api/stripe-webhook.ts — that's owned by another team.
- Make sure we keep the existing cart_v2 cookie name and never store PII in the payload.

[handoff]
- to=any    do=The next step is to add a regression test in tests/checkout_refresh.spec.ts covering the post-redirect refresh path.

